From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Drop a message posted to the PS5 desktop window.

A game crashed when a controller was first used: Slay the Spire's audio
thread read a null pointer and the process ended.

DirectInput notes input activity by posting WM_USER, with 0 and 0, to
the desktop window, at most once a second. On a desktop Wine explorer
owns that window and reads the message. On the PS5 the server creates
the window and no process serves it. Its handle still names the first
thread that asked for it, so the post lands in that thread's queue. In
Slay the Spire that thread is OpenAL Soft's message thread. Its
GetMessage takes WM_USER..WM_USER+5 and treats WM_USER as "open a
device", whose device pointer is lParam: 0.

This process holds no WND for the desktop or the message-only window, so
nothing here can run their procedures (see patch 0967 for sent
messages). A message posted to either now goes nowhere and the post
succeeds, as it would once explorer had read it. Only those two handles
are matched: a message-only window a program creates (parent
HWND_MESSAGE) is a window of its own and still gets its messages, as
does every other window and every thread. The first drop is logged as a
warning, each one as a trace on the msg channel.
---
 dlls/win32u/message.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/message.c b/dlls/win32u/message.c
index 734b72df9c..a34e28f00a 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/message.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/message.c
@@ -4726,6 +4726,23 @@ BOOL WINAPI NtUserPostMessage( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam
 
     if (!hwnd) return NtUserPostThreadMessage( GetCurrentThreadId(), msg, wparam, lparam );
 
+#ifdef WINE_PS5_USER_DRIVER
+    /* no explorer serves the server-created desktop or the message-only window:
+     * their handles still name the thread that first asked for them, so a
+     * message posted to either reaches that thread's GetMessage, which can take
+     * it for one of its own. This process holds no WND for them and can't run
+     * their procedures: the post goes nowhere, as explorer would have read it. */
+    cache_thread_desktop_windows();
+    if (get_user_thread_info()->top_window && is_desktop_window( hwnd ))
+    {
+        static LONG warned;
+        if (!InterlockedExchange( &warned, 1 ))
+            WARN( "dropping messages posted to the desktop window, first %p msg %x\n", hwnd, msg );
+        TRACE( "dropped hwnd %p msg %x wp %lx lp %lx\n", hwnd, msg, (long)wparam, lparam );
+        return TRUE;
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (!(info.dest_tid = get_window_thread( hwnd, NULL ))) return FALSE;
 
     if (is_exiting_thread( info.dest_tid )) return TRUE;
